  "query_preview": "..\nThe big story, TS Champi. Champi continues to slowly strengthen east\nof Guam as it moves west. The latest forecast track brings Champi\nover northern Guam Sunday morning, with tropical storm force winds\narriving before midnight Saturday. Therefore, a Typhoon Warning was \nissued for Guam and Rota, with a Tropical Storm Warning issued for \nTinian and Saipan, with a Typhoon Watch continuing in case Champi \nmakes a turn to the north. The forecast for tonight and Saturday \nmaintains the current drier pattern. However, that will change \ndrastically as Champi approaches. Tropical storm force winds, \nincreasing heavy showers and thunderstorms will move into the region \nSaturday evening. By Sunday morning, we can expect at least category \n2 typhoon force winds at Guam, category 1 at Rota and strong tropical\nstorm winds at Tinian and Saipan. Winds and convection will continue\nover the islands through Sunday night, with tropical storm \nconditions possibly ending Sunday night, after midnight. After Champi\nexits the region, a dry pattern looks to move into the region around\nMonday and continuing through the end of the week. Residents of the \nMarianas should make sure that they are prepared for typhoon force\nsustained winds of up to 105 mph. Stay safe and follow our forecasts\nfor any updates as they occur.",
